\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  Why should sorrow ever grieve me?\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Christ is near, what can here
\par E'er of Him deprive me?
\par Rob me of my place in heaven
\par That God's  Son, as my own,
\par Unto me hath given?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Satan world and all its pleasure
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I forsake, gladly take
\par Scorn, yet hold my treasure
\par All their laughter, their derision,
\par God my strength, will at length
\par Change to indecision.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. What is all that man posseses?
\par But a handful of sand
\par that the heart distresses.
\par \pard   There are gifts that perish never,
\par    \cf1 Christ gives me all these free\cf0 
\par    to enjoy for ever.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Shepherd! Lord! Joy's fountain ever!
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thou art mine, I am Thine,
\par no one can us sever.
\par I am thine because Thou gavest
\par life and blood for my good,
\par by Thy death Thou savest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Thou art mine and I confess Thee
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Ne'er shall I, Light of joy,
\par From my heart dethrone Thee
\par Let me, let me soon behold Thee
\par face to face, Thy embrace
\par may for e'er enfold me!
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

